cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, the live platform, or any derived product from Abyssal Claims, please cite the Zenodo deposit below."
title: "Abyssal Claims: source code of an integration platform for ocean and land environmental data"
abstract: >-
  Abyssal Claims is an independently developed, non-commercial web platform that
  brings more than fifty publicly funded environmental datasets together on one
  interactive three-dimensional map. It began with deep-sea mining and has grown
  into a working space for ocean and land data, from individual measurements and
  biodiversity records to seabed contracts and the land-side impacts of mining.
  Its purpose is to let researchers and other stakeholders explore how these
  datasets relate: a measurement beside the gridded field it informs, a
  concession beside the species recorded inside it, and the places where the
  ocean has hardly been observed at all.
  This repository contains the platform source code (React + deck.gl
  frontend, FastAPI + PostGIS backend, and the data-sync pipelines). The platform's
  datasets are not included: each layer is fetched at runtime from its upstream
  provider under that provider's own licence. The only data in the repository are
  small verbatim excerpts used by the parser tests (about 5 MB in
  backend/tests/fixtures/), which stay under their upstream licences; see
  DATA-LICENCES.md. The accompanying Zenodo deposit documents the data sources,
  refresh strategies, architecture, derived products, known limitations and
  licensing model.
type: software
# `version` is the SOFTWARE release, deliberately independent of the documentation
# deposit's version. Do not sync the two — they have different
# cadences; that separation is the whole reason the code gets its own Zenodo record.
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
